{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Observe the month of the aviv.</b> It is the month of Nisan, in which there was aviv when they went out of Egypt. And the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: watch it before it comes, that it be fit for aviv to bring the omer in it; and if not, intercalate the year." "<b>From Egypt, night.</b> The taking out was by day, as it is said (Numbers 33): ״ממחרת הפסח יצאו בני ישראל״, and it is written (Exodus 12): ״בעצם היום הזה יצאו״. But from the hour they were permitted to leave, at night, it is called a 'taking out.' Therefore Scripture did not say 'בלילה' (in the night) but 'לילה' (night), to allude to the hour they were permitted, as it is said (ibid.): ״ויקרא למשה ולאהרן לילה ויאמר קומו צאו״, and therefore Onkelos translated: ועבד לך נסין בליליא — 'and I performed miracles for you in the night' — so that you should not understand that the taking out was at night."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:37.251130909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}